", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's governor race pairs first-term incumbent Josh Shapiro against Republican state Treasurer Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Shapiro has led every independent poll of the cycle by double digits, including recent surveys showing margins of 17 to 27 points, and averages put his lead around 22 points. All seven expert raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets give Shapiro roughly a 97 percent chance of winning.\n\nGarrity has struggled to attract the outside spending she hoped would arrive in the campaign's final weeks, and the only debate comes late in October. A Libertarian candidate may shave a few points off the totals. The race sits in a politically competitive state, but Shapiro's personal standing and the polling gap make him a heavy favorite for reelection.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9964, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9934, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 20.0}]}